From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] spirv: a 16-bit shader input or output declares the StorageInputOutput16 capability

SpirvBuilder emits 16-bit input and output variables without the
StorageInputOutput16 capability that allows them, so the module uses a
feature it does not declare (spirv-val does not flag it) and a driver may
run it without having enabled that feature. emitDclIoVar now enables the
capability for an f16, i16 or u16 I/O variable. Applied to DXVK's
subprojects/dxbc-spirv by tools/build_d3d_runtime.sh; goes with
dxvk-patches/0017.
---
diff --git a/spirv/spirv_builder.cpp b/spirv/spirv_builder.cpp
index c43a987..36b4d46 100644
--- a/spirv/spirv_builder.cpp
+++ b/spirv/spirv_builder.cpp
@@ -855,6 +855,12 @@ void SpirvBuilder::emitDclIoVar(const ir::Op& op) {
   uint32_t typeId = getIdForType(op.getType());
   uint32_t varId = getIdForDef(op.getDef());
 
+  /* A 16-bit input or output is storage the device must have enabled */
+  auto ioScalar = op.getType().getBaseType(0u).getBaseType();
+
+  if (ioScalar == ir::ScalarType::eF16 || ioScalar == ir::ScalarType::eI16 || ioScalar == ir::ScalarType::eU16)
+    enableCapability(spv::CapabilityStorageInputOutput16);
+
   emitDebugName(op.getDef(), varId);
 
   uint32_t ptrTypeId = getIdForPtrType(typeId, storageClass);
